  <node unique_id="9" master_id="0" name="Technical Specification &amp; Database Reference" prog_lang="custom-colors" tags="" readonly="0" nosearch_me="0" nosearch_ch="0" custom_icon_id="0" is_bold="0" foreground="" ts_creation="1793782569" ts_lastsave="1795335102">
    <rich_text>
</rich_text>
    <rich_text scale="h1">TECHNICAL SPECIFICATION &amp; DATABASE REFERENCE</rich_text>
    <rich_text>

</rich_text>
    <rich_text scale="h2">1. Data Dictionary &amp; Database Schema</rich_text>
    <rich_text>
</rich_text>
    <rich_text weight="heavy">Database:</rich_text>
    <rich_text> </rich_text>
    <rich_text family="monospace">schemax_sis</rich_text>
    <rich_text>
</rich_text>
    <rich_text weight="heavy">DBMS:</rich_text>
    <rich_text> MySQL 8.x
</rich_text>
    <rich_text weight="heavy">Port:</rich_text>
    <rich_text> 3306
The system uses five main database tables:
</rich_text>
    <rich_text weight="heavy">users</rich_text>
    <rich_text>
• </rich_text>
    <rich_text family="monospace">user_id</rich_text>
    <rich_text> — INT, Primary Key, Auto Increment

• </rich_text>
    <rich_text family="monospace">first_name</rich_text>
    <rich_text>, </rich_text>
    <rich_text family="monospace">surname</rich_text>
    <rich_text> — VARCHAR(100)

• </rich_text>
    <rich_text family="monospace">bu_email</rich_text>
    <rich_text> — VARCHAR(255)

• </rich_text>
    <rich_text family="monospace">username</rich_text>
    <rich_text> — VARCHAR(100)

• </rich_text>
    <rich_text family="monospace">password_hash</rich_text>
    <rich_text> — VARCHAR(255)


</rich_text>
    <rich_text weight="heavy">students</rich_text>
    <rich_text>
◇ </rich_text>
    <rich_text family="monospace">student_id</rich_text>
    <rich_text> — VARCHAR(15), Primary Key

◇ </rich_text>
    <rich_text family="monospace">first_name</rich_text>
    <rich_text>, </rich_text>
    <rich_text family="monospace">middle_name</rich_text>
    <rich_text>, </rich_text>
    <rich_text family="monospace">surname</rich_text>
    <rich_text> — VARCHAR(50)

◇ </rich_text>
    <rich_text family="monospace">gender</rich_text>
    <rich_text> — ENUM

◇ </rich_text>
    <rich_text family="monospace">year_level</rich_text>
    <rich_text> — TINYINT

◇ </rich_text>
    <rich_text family="monospace">program</rich_text>
    <rich_text> — VARCHAR(50)

◇ </rich_text>
    <rich_text family="monospace">bloc</rich_text>
    <rich_text> — VARCHAR(10)

◇ </rich_text>
    <rich_text family="monospace">birthday</rich_text>
    <rich_text> — DATE

◇ </rich_text>
    <rich_text family="monospace">bu_email</rich_text>
    <rich_text> — VARCHAR(100)

◇ </rich_text>
    <rich_text family="monospace">contact_no</rich_text>
    <rich_text> — VARCHAR(20)

◇ </rich_text>
    <rich_text family="monospace">photo_path</rich_text>
    <rich_text> — VARCHAR(300)

◇ </rich_text>
    <rich_text family="monospace">created_at</rich_text>
    <rich_text> — TIMESTAMP

◇ </rich_text>
    <rich_text family="monospace">user_id</rich_text>
    <rich_text> — INT


</rich_text>
    <rich_text weight="heavy">subjects</rich_text>
    <rich_text>
◇ </rich_text>
    <rich_text family="monospace">subject_id</rich_text>
    <rich_text> — INT, Primary Key, Auto Increment

◇ </rich_text>
    <rich_text family="monospace">subject_code</rich_text>
    <rich_text> — VARCHAR(15)

◇ </rich_text>
    <rich_text family="monospace">title</rich_text>
    <rich_text> — VARCHAR(100)

◇ </rich_text>
    <rich_text family="monospace">units</rich_text>
    <rich_text> — TINYINT


</rich_text>
    <rich_text weight="heavy">student_subjects</rich_text>
    <rich_text>
◇ </rich_text>
    <rich_text family="monospace">id</rich_text>
    <rich_text> — INT, Primary Key, Auto Increment

◇ </rich_text>
    <rich_text family="monospace">student_id</rich_text>
    <rich_text> — VARCHAR(15)

◇ </rich_text>
    <rich_text family="monospace">subject_id</rich_text>
    <rich_text> — INT

◇ </rich_text>
    <rich_text family="monospace">grade</rich_text>
    <rich_text> — DECIMAL(3,2)


</rich_text>
    <rich_text weight="heavy">attendance</rich_text>
    <rich_text>
◇ </rich_text>
    <rich_text family="monospace">attendance_id</rich_text>
    <rich_text> — INT, Primary Key, Auto Increment

◇ </rich_text>
    <rich_text family="monospace">student_id</rich_text>
    <rich_text> — VARCHAR(15)

◇ </rich_text>
    <rich_text family="monospace">subject_id</rich_text>
    <rich_text> — INT

◇ </rich_text>
    <rich_text family="monospace">attendance_date</rich_text>
    <rich_text> — DATE

◇ </rich_text>
    <rich_text family="monospace">status</rich_text>
    <rich_text> — ENUM


</rich_text>
    <rich_text weight="heavy">Relationships:</rich_text>
    <rich_text> </rich_text>
    <rich_text family="monospace">student_subjects</rich_text>
    <rich_text> and </rich_text>
    <rich_text family="monospace">attendance</rich_text>
    <rich_text> associate student and subject records. The </rich_text>
    <rich_text family="monospace">students</rich_text>
    <rich_text> table also contains an optional </rich_text>
    <rich_text family="monospace">user_id</rich_text>
    <rich_text> reference. Actual database-enforced foreign keys and indexes should be checked against </rich_text>
    <rich_text family="monospace">db/schemax_sis.sql</rich_text>
    <rich_text>.


</rich_text>
    <rich_text scale="h2">2. Desktop Analytics Implementation</rich_text>
    <rich_text>
</rich_text>
    <rich_text weight="heavy">Framework:</rich_text>
    <rich_text> C# Windows Forms (.NET 10)
</rich_text>
    <rich_text weight="heavy">Library:</rich_text>
    <rich_text> ScottPlot
</rich_text>
    <rich_text weight="heavy">Source File:</rich_text>
    <rich_text> </rich_text>
    <rich_text family="monospace">dashboardForm.cs</rich_text>
    <rich_text>
The desktop dashboard retrieves student records from MySQL and generates bar charts showing students per year level and per program. The Refresh Dashboard function retrieves updated database statistics and redraws the charts.
</rich_text>
    <rich_text weight="heavy">ScottPlot initialization and styling (excerpt):</rich_text>
    <rich_text>
</rich_text>
    <rich_text family="monospace">_yearPlot.Plot.Clear();
_yearPlot.Plot.Title("Students per Year Level", size: 12);

var bars = new List&lt;ScottPlot.Bar&gt;();
var ticks = new List&lt;ScottPlot.Tick&gt;();
int i = 0;

foreach (var kv in perYear)
{
    bars.Add(new ScottPlot.Bar
    {
        Position = i,
        Value = kv.Value,
        FillColor = ScottPlot.Color.FromHex("#33658A"),
        Label = kv.Value.ToString()
    });

    ticks.Add(new ScottPlot.Tick(i, $"Yr {kv.Key}"));
    i++;
}

var barPlot = _yearPlot.Plot.Add.Bars(bars);
barPlot.ValueLabelStyle.IsVisible = true;
barPlot.ValueLabelStyle.FontSize = 10;</rich_text>
    <rich_text weight="heavy">SQL aggregation example:</rich_text>
    <rich_text>
</rich_text>
    <rich_text family="monospace">SELECT year_level, COUNT(*) AS total
FROM students
GROUP BY year_level
ORDER BY year_level;</rich_text>
    <rich_text>The SQL query groups students by year level. The resulting counts can be displayed as ScottPlot bars. This is an illustrative aggregation query; the actual dashboard query should be checked against the source code.


</rich_text>
    <rich_text scale="h2">3. Mobile Application Architecture</rich_text>
    <rich_text>
</rich_text>
    <rich_text weight="heavy">Framework:</rich_text>
    <rich_text> .NET MAUI (.NET 10)
</rich_text>
    <rich_text weight="heavy">Language:</rich_text>
    <rich_text> C#
</rich_text>
    <rich_text weight="heavy">Interface:</rich_text>
    <rich_text> XAML
</rich_text>
    <rich_text weight="heavy">Database Library:</rich_text>
    <rich_text> MySqlConnector
The Android application provides a student directory with navigation, search, and database operations. It uses asynchronous MySQL access to avoid blocking the user interface.
</rich_text>
    <rich_text weight="heavy">Database connection configuration:</rich_text>
    <rich_text>
◇ Android emulator: </rich_text>
    <rich_text family="monospace">10.0.2.2</rich_text>
    <rich_text>

◇ Physical Android device: reachable MySQL server IP address

◇ MySQL port: </rich_text>
    <rich_text family="monospace">3306</rich_text>
    <rich_text>

◇ Database: </rich_text>
    <rich_text family="monospace">schemax_sis</rich_text>
    <rich_text>


</rich_text>
    <rich_text weight="heavy">Asynchronous MySQL pattern (illustrative):</rich_text>
    <rich_text>
</rich_text>
    <rich_text family="monospace">await using var connection =
    new MySqlConnection(connectionString);

await connection.OpenAsync();

await using var command =
    new MySqlCommand(
        "SELECT * FROM students", connection);

await using var reader =
    await command.ExecuteReaderAsync();</rich_text>
    <rich_text weight="heavy">XAML CollectionView card template (illustrative):</rich_text>
    <rich_text>
</rich_text>
    <rich_text family="monospace">&lt;CollectionView ItemsSource="{Binding Students}"&gt;
    &lt;CollectionView.ItemTemplate&gt;
        &lt;DataTemplate&gt;
            &lt;Border Padding="10" Margin="5"&gt;
                &lt;VerticalStackLayout&gt;
                    &lt;Label Text="{Binding StudentId}" /&gt;
                    &lt;Label Text="{Binding FullName}" /&gt;
                &lt;/VerticalStackLayout&gt;
            &lt;/Border&gt;
        &lt;/DataTemplate&gt;
    &lt;/CollectionView.ItemTemplate&gt;
&lt;/CollectionView&gt;</rich_text>
    <rich_text>The CollectionView displays student records using a reusable card layout. The actual property names and bindings should match the project's view model.

</rich_text>
    <rich_text weight="heavy">Cross-Platform Data Consistency:</rich_text>
    <rich_text> Both applications access the shared MySQL database. Updates become visible when the other application retrieves or refreshes its records.
</rich_text>
    <rich_text weight="heavy">Security:</rich_text>
    <rich_text> Database credentials must remain confidential. Direct MySQL connections should be restricted to trusted networks; a secured backend API is recommended for production deployment.
</rich_text>
