  <node unique_id="10" master_id="0" name="System Administration &amp; Deployment Guide" prog_lang="custom-colors" tags="" readonly="0" nosearch_me="0" nosearch_ch="0" custom_icon_id="0" is_bold="0" foreground="" ts_creation="1793782600" ts_lastsave="1795335574">
    <rich_text>
</rich_text>
    <rich_text scale="h1">SYSTEM ADMINISTRATION &amp; DEPLOYMENT GUIDE</rich_text>
    <rich_text>

</rich_text>
    <rich_text scale="h2">1. Server &amp; Environment Prerequisites</rich_text>
    <rich_text>
</rich_text>
    <rich_text weight="heavy">Desktop Application:</rich_text>
    <rich_text>
• Windows 10/11

• .NET 10 Desktop Runtime

• MySQL Server 8.x

• MySQL port: 3306

• Configured database: </rich_text>
    <rich_text family="monospace">schemax_sis</rich_text>
    <rich_text>


</rich_text>
    <rich_text weight="heavy">Mobile Application:</rich_text>
    <rich_text>
◇ Compatible Android device or emulator

◇ .NET MAUI Android application

◇ Network access to the MySQL server

◇ Valid database credentials


</rich_text>
    <rich_text weight="heavy">Database Configuration:</rich_text>
    <rich_text>
◇ Execute </rich_text>
    <rich_text family="monospace">db/schemax_sis.sql</rich_text>
    <rich_text> to create the database.

◇ Execute </rich_text>
    <rich_text family="monospace">db/02_capstone_seed.sql</rich_text>
    <rich_text> to insert sample records if needed.

◇ Configure the appropriate MySQL account and connection settings.


</rich_text>
    <rich_text weight="heavy">Network Addresses:</rich_text>
    <rich_text>
◇ Windows local database: </rich_text>
    <rich_text family="monospace">localhost</rich_text>
    <rich_text>

◇ Android emulator: </rich_text>
    <rich_text family="monospace">10.0.2.2</rich_text>
    <rich_text>

◇ Physical Android device: MySQL server's reachable LAN IP address


The MySQL service must be running, and firewall rules must allow authorized connections.

</rich_text>
    <rich_text scale="h2">2. Desktop Setup Package (MSI/EXE)</rich_text>
    <rich_text>
</rich_text>
    <rich_text weight="heavy">Release:</rich_text>
    <rich_text> SchemaX SIS v1.1.0
</rich_text>
    <rich_text weight="heavy">Installation Files:</rich_text>
    <rich_text>
◇ </rich_text>
    <rich_text family="monospace">SchemaX.SIS.Setup.msi</rich_text>
    <rich_text>

◇ </rich_text>
    <rich_text family="monospace">setup.exe</rich_text>
    <rich_text>


</rich_text>
    <rich_text weight="heavy">Build Procedure:</rich_text>
    <rich_text>
1. Open the SchemaX.SIS solution in Visual Studio.

2. Build the Windows Forms application.

3. Build the </rich_text>
    <rich_text family="monospace">SchemaX.SIS.Setup</rich_text>
    <rich_text> installer project.

4. Verify that the MSI and setup executable are generated.

</rich_text>
    <rich_text weight="heavy">Installation Procedure:</rich_text>
    <rich_text>
1. Download both installer files from the GitHub release.

2. Keep both files in the same folder.

3. Run </rich_text>
    <rich_text family="monospace">setup.exe</rich_text>
    <rich_text> and follow the installation wizard.

4. Launch SchemaX SIS and verify database connectivity.

</rich_text>
    <rich_text weight="heavy">Uninstallation:</rich_text>
    <rich_text> Remove SchemaX SIS through Windows Settings → Apps → Installed Apps.


</rich_text>
    <rich_text scale="h2">3. Mobile Keystore &amp; APK Packaging</rich_text>
    <rich_text>
</rich_text>
    <rich_text weight="heavy">Framework:</rich_text>
    <rich_text> .NET MAUI (.NET 10)
</rich_text>
    <rich_text weight="heavy">Platform:</rich_text>
    <rich_text> Android
</rich_text>
    <rich_text weight="heavy">Release Package:</rich_text>
    <rich_text> </rich_text>
    <rich_text family="monospace">SchemaX-SIS-Final-v2.apk</rich_text>
    <rich_text>
</rich_text>
    <rich_text weight="heavy">Packaging Procedure:</rich_text>
    <rich_text>
1. Open </rich_text>
    <rich_text family="monospace">SchemaX.Mobile</rich_text>
    <rich_text> in Visual Studio.

2. Select the Release configuration.

3. Configure Android APK signing with the project's keystore.

4. Build or publish the signed APK.

5. Verify that the APK is successfully generated and signed.

</rich_text>
    <rich_text weight="heavy">Installation Procedure:</rich_text>
    <rich_text>
1. Transfer the APK to an Android device.

2. Allow installation from the selected trusted source if prompted.

3. Install and launch the application.

4. Configure the MySQL server address and authorized credentials.

5. Verify that student records can be retrieved.


</rich_text>
    <rich_text weight="heavy">Security &amp; Troubleshooting:</rich_text>
    <rich_text>
◇ Never publish keystore passwords or database credentials.

◇ Keep signing keys in a secure location.

◇ If the desktop application cannot connect, check MySQL, firewall rules, and connection settings.

◇ If Android cannot connect, verify the server IP address, port 3306, and network connectivity.

◇ If installation fails, check device compatibility, APK integrity, and signing configuration.


</rich_text>
    <rich_text weight="heavy">Release Reference:</rich_text>
    <rich_text> </rich_text>
    <rich_text link="webs https://github.com/reynalynsaavedrasamar25/SchemaX-SIS/releases/tag/v1.1.0">https://github.com/reynalynsaavedrasamar25/SchemaX-SIS/releases/tag/v1.1.0</rich_text>
    <rich_text>
</rich_text>
    <encoded_png char_offset="1511" justification="left" link=""></encoded_png>
